			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates with macOS UX fixes and extension webview support\n\nSynchronize five Element submodules to their latest downstream versions delivering critical macOS UX improvements and extension webview infrastructure:\n\n- Mountain (fb254ade, 54650acd): Fix boot race and close handling for macOS (Cmd+W intercept, DevTools focus opt-in) and add vscode-webview:// URI scheme handler for extension webviews (Roo Code, Claude, GitLens)\n- Output (0d474607): Add macOS titlebar offset and z-index CSS transforms, expand sandbox stripping to both iframe sites, rewrite webview shell CSP\n- Sky (1270c609): Add window close handler (Cmd+W closes active editor first), lifecycle focus after restoration, and opt-in command catalog smoke test\n- Wind (31a0dd9f): Update service layer with latest Effect-TS changes\n\nThese fixes resolve the \"I can't type or keybind\" issue, empty Explorer on first launch, and enable sideloaded extension webviews to render properly.",
			"SHA": "0ebddba9c443930843c63da5c57e55c771d63970"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T18:59:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				7
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates with dependency bumps and Mountain extension roots\n\nSynchronize seven Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\n- Cocoon: Bump OpenTelemetry devDependencies (sdk-trace-node, exporter-trace-otlp-http, sdk-trace-base, sdk-logs, sdk-metrics, sdk-trace-web)\n- Common: Bump @cloudflare/workers-types to 4.20260430.1\n- Echo: Bump @cloudflare/workers-types to 4.20260430.1\n- Mountain: Revert to simple Mountain naming and add extension_root allowlist for Land and VSCode extension directories\n- Wind: Bump OpenTelemetry devDependencies and reformat ESBuild config/output to readable multi-line format\n- Worker: Bump @types/serviceworker and expand ESBuild configuration from minified to readable format\n- Output: Sync point\n\nThe Mountain extension_root allowlist enables the `/Extension/<abs-fs-path>` URL prefix to serve extension-contributed assets (icons, webview resources) from ~/.land/extensions and ~/.vscode/extensions, fixing missing icons for sideloaded extensions like GitLens.",
			"SHA": "a685e1ad979c05f8388ed015296baba853e5558d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:24:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Add codegen entry point and public exports\n\nAdd the runnable CLI entry point (Codegen.ts) that invokes the extension-host codegen pipeline and the public module surface (index.ts) re-exporting all types and functions.\n\nCodegen.ts is invoked by Cocoon's prepublishOnly.sh build hook. It resolves source/output paths from process.cwd() pointing to the VS Code editor source tree and the Cocoon output directory respectively. The implementation handles exit codes: non-zero for internal failures, exit code 2 for codegen failures, and exits cleanly on success with a summary of records emitted and duration.\n\nindex.ts exports the full public API including RunExtHostCodegen orchestrator and its options/summary types, IterateExtHostDecorators async iterator and IsExtHostFile predicate, EmitExtHostSchema emitter with its options/outcome types, and ExtHostDecoratorRecord type.\n\nThis completes the codegen infrastructure added in the previous commit, making it callable from the build system.",
			"SHA": "4aad2b476a55865e9e4eeb58d471f4d576e28cd7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:22:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule updates with extension-host codegen and bridge shape generation\n\nSynchronize three Element submodules to their latest downstream versions delivering Phase-3 codegen pipeline completion:\n\n- Cocoon (1db2b302): Add extension-host codegen infrastructure mirroring Wind's ServiceSchema codegen but targeting the extHost decorator family. New Extract/IsExtHostFile.ts filters to `vs/workbench/api/*/extHost*.ts`, IterateExtHostDecorators.ts resolves cross-file interfaces and records paired MainThread counterparts, EmitExtHostSchema.ts emits schema files under `Cocoon/Source/Effect/Generated/<Decorator>/`, and RunExtHostCodegen.ts orchestrates the pipeline. Reuses Wind extractors verbatim - no parser duplication.\n\n- Mountain (3f0b6908): Rename binary and library to verbose production profile name (ProductionNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Compile_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain). Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier to match, and add duplicate Binary/node entry to externalBin for production node path. Supports multi-profile build pipeline for development vs production builds.\n\n- Wind (5de2328c): Phase-3 codegen pipeline adds bridge shape generation - EmitBridgeShape.ts generates `Pick<...Upstream, ...>` bridge shape files derived from codegen-emitted upstream schemas, eliminating hand-maintained bridge shapes. WorkbenchBridgeShapeManifest provides curated narrowing of 18 upstream members per service. Also adds WorkbenchProductService (IProductService bridge) and WorkbenchProgressService (IProgressService with location handling). LandWorkbenchLayer and Tags updated. prepublishOnly.sh now runs codegen before production build.",
			"SHA": "d1b4f7ebb7f67523e4d7ba78221297ca481ce5fb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:16:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain,Wind): Sync submodule updates with layout/extension services and build config\n\nSynchronize Mountain and Wind submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\nMountain (20b9363): Revert production profile names to simple Mountain identifier - restore binary, library, and default-run targets to use \"Mountain\" instead of verbose production profile string. Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier, remove duplicate externalBin entry, and delete redundant backup files.\n\nWind (12507057): Add four new workbench-tier Effect-TS service layers:\n- WorkbenchContextKeyService: Context key value management and expression evaluation\n- WorkbenchExtensionService: Extension activation and snapshot management\n- WorkbenchLayoutService: Workbench part visibility controls (ActivityBar, Sidebar, Panel, StatusBar)\n- WorkbenchProgressProblem: Problem ADT for progress task failures\n- Complete WorkbenchEditorService with Live implementation for pane management\n\nAll services follow Wind's established pattern with BridgeShape, Service, Tag, Problem ADT, and Live runtime bridge implementation via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES_.",
			"SHA": "d0eeeb8b75ced8842c1a7bbcb69d3a4884f74d5c"
		}
